<title>GERMANY: Netanyahu lands in Germany for one-day visit.</title>
<headline>Netanyahu lands in Germany for one-day visit.</headline>
<dateline>HANOVER, Germany 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu arrived in Germany on Thursday for a one-day visit during which he will lay a wreath at the Bergen-Belsen concentration camp.</p>
<p>Netanyahu's plane arrived from Paris in the northern city of Hanover just after 8 a.m. (0600 GMT) and his delegation was due to be flown by helicopter to Bergen-Belsen before he goes on to Bonn for talks with Chancellor Helmut Kohl.</p>
</text>
